#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Idempotent write-path probe for the LastDB canary soak gate.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-08-05): the 24h soak is the last gate before a public
# Homebrew stable release, and every one of its hard checks was a liveness or a
# read check — `launchctl print`, `lastdb status`, `kanban ping`, `situations
# list`. Not one of them wrote. A candidate whose board writes ran ~4s (vs
# ~1.2s) soaked green on all four while `brain put` took 3.9s on 3 of 3 samples.
# The write path was the only thing that build broke, and it was the only thing
# the gate could not see.
#
# The probe is ONE upsert of ONE fixed slug. It is idempotent by construction —
# the same slug, the same constant body, every tick — so repeating it hourly
# neither grows the store nor changes any meaning. It goes through the ordinary
# LastDB mutation path, which is exactly the path under test.
#
# Passive alternatives were considered and rejected: `lastdb status` reports
# `app=kanban verb=mutation avg=/p95=`, but on 2026-08-05 that surface read
# p95=224ms while direct probes measured 3.9s on every sample. An average over
# a restart-scoped ring is not a trustworthy bar; a timed write is.
#
# Prints nothing on success. The CALLER does the timing and enforces the bound
# (see CHECK_BUDGET_MS in last-stack-canary-pipeline) — keeping the bar in the
# pipeline means one place decides what "too slow" means.
set -euo pipefail

SLUG="${LAST_STACK_CANARY_WRITE_PROBE_SLUG:-canary-soak-write-probe}"
BRAIN="${LAST_STACK_CANARY_BRAIN_CMD:-brain}"

# Frontmatter MUST open and close with standalone `---` lines; `brain put`
# exits 2 on bare `type:`/`slug:`/`title:` keys without the fences.
"$BRAIN" put >/dev/null <<EOF
---
type: reference
slug: ${SLUG}
title: Canary soak write-path probe (constant body; carries no meaning)
---

Written by the LastDB canary soak gate's \`board_write\` check to time the
primary's write path. The body is deliberately constant — the only thing that
matters is how long the mutation takes, not what it says.

Safe to delete at any time; the next soak-watch tick recreates it. Rationale:
brain \`papercut-canary-soak-gate-has-no-write-path-check\`.
EOF
